From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:15:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 245/260] [ae-patch] Let the transcript keep ignore the
 server's own resource and error items

The progress record behind the cold-relaunch transcript keep went stale live: the server adds
a resource_event item right after every relaunch, and the keep treated any item the forwarder
had not posted as foreign, so no record ever advanced and every relaunch rebuilt.

Item types the rebuild leaves out of the transcript (reasoning, error, native_tool,
resource_event, routing_decision, slash_command, terminal_command) no longer block the record
and no longer force a rebuild when they trail it. Any other type, including a missing or
unknown one, still counts as part of the transcript. The keep now checks that the recorded
last item still sits at its recorded position and that everything after it is a skipped type,
and a kept or copied transcript moves its record up to the server's end.
